description: 'v028''s exact recipe -- same architecture, same distill_weight 1.0,
  same teacher, same seed -- with ONE change: training.epochs 3 -> 5. 225,922 params,
  so the latency profile is identical to v028 and inherited by construction.'
hypothesis: 'The local-to-public offset is NOT a constant, and it moves with training
  length. Measured across six scored submissions, five 3-epoch runs share an offset
  of -0.028264 +/- 0.000419. v025 -- the only 5-epoch run -- sits at -0.026438, which
  is +0.001826 from that mean, or +4.4 sigma. The control is unusually clean: v024
  is the SAME recipe as v025 at 3 epochs and sits normally at -0.028818, so batch
  64 is exonerated and epochs is the only structural difference. Against v024 specifically
  the shift is +0.002380.

  The consequence is that full_valid_wp is a BIASED selector across different training
  lengths, biased against the longer run. v025 was ranked a -1.5 sigma local regression
  and was therefore nearly discarded, yet it scored 0.6580 public and beat v023 (0.6568)
  by +0.0012. Local selection actively mis-ranked it.

  So combine the two things that are known to help. v028 has the best local score
  in the project (0.686510, +11.5 sigma) and carries the standard offset. v025 demonstrates
  a +0.0024 public uplift from training longer. If the two compose, the prediction
  is 0.6585 + 0.0024 = 0.6609, against a 0.6677 leader where we currently sit 0.0092
  back.

  Falsifiable and stated as such: this predicts a public score near 0.6609. If the
  run instead lands at v028''s 0.6585, the epoch effect did not transfer to this recipe
  and the offset shift was specific to v025''s lower distillation weight -- which
  would be a genuinely interesting distinction, since it would mean the two levers
  interact rather than add.'
change_vs_parent: training.epochs 3 -> 5 only. distill_weight stays 1.0, gamma stays
  absent, params, hidden, input_proj, chunk_len, teacher, schedule, LR and seed are
  all unchanged, so this isolates training length against v028 rather than against
  v025.
